result:
Full test of 1.21.0 on portable VS Code 1.146.0 with vscode-mcp 0.9.1 (the 2026-10-28 row was a smoke test). pythonIndent.newlineAndIndent driven via run_command - the command the Enter keybinding invokes; the when-clause gating itself (suggestWidgetVisible, vim/neovim modes, multi-cursor) is untested. Verified: bracket alignment puts the next line right of the open bracket ({'a': -> 12 spaces inside a def), nested [[ aligns to the inner bracket (14 spaces, matching the README example), and after 'c': 5} the indent returns to the pre-bracket level; hanging indent full (my_func( -> indented line, ) on its own line) and partial (content right of cursor -> line indent + tabSize only); keepHangingBracketOnLine=true keeps ) on the indented line (my_func() -> "(
    )"), false puts it on its own ("(

)"); else: dedents the current line and indents the next, and the nested-else case correctly does NOT dedent; Enter mid-comment continues the comment ("    # This function is |gonna" -> next line "    # gonna..."); backslash continuation indents +tabSize; whitespace right of the cursor is trimmed (def f(x,| y): -> "y):" aligned under "x"); trimLinesWithOnlyWhitespace=true empties a whitespace-only line, false preserves it; a non-python file falls back to a plain newline. STILL PRESENT, already filed: issue #135 reproduces in 1.21.0 - a comment ending in ( still hanging-indents ("    # (" + Enter -> 8 spaces instead of 4); shouldHang in out/parser.js reads line[char-1] with no comment stripping. Not tested: useTabOnHangingIndent's Tab jump (needs a real Tab keypress; the setting only swaps the snippet cursor placeholder $0->$1), elif/except/finally variants (same code path as else). Harness note: insertSnippet is async - get_text in the same batch can return pre-edit text; re-read after a short wait (a same-batch read once showed the file unchanged while the edit was still landing, which looked like a defect and was not).
